{"title":"2017 UNM-PNM Statewide High School Mathematics Contest II Problems","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p>UNM - PNM STATEWIDE MATHEMATICS CONTEST XLIX. February 4, 2017. Second Round. Three Hours\n</p>\n<div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Problem_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Problem_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Problem_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Problem_5\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 5</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Problem_6\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 6</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Problem_7\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 7</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Problem_8\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 8</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Problem_9\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 9</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#Problem_10\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">10</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 10</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-11\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">11</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_1\">Problem 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_UNM-PNM_Statewide_High_School_Mathematics_Contest_II_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>What are the last two digits of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/0/0/c002566606b9154bc641f7538defc73bdb8f91d7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2017^{2017}$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"62\" height=\"15\" />?\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_UNM-PNM_Statewide_High_School_Mathematics_Contest_II_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2017 UNM-PNM Statewide High School Mathematics Contest II Problems/Problem 1\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_2\">Problem 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_UNM-PNM_Statewide_High_School_Mathematics_Contest_II_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Suppose <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/9/7/9970c215805f82282067d60741f7d2625e4d6a0c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A, R, S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"55\" height=\"16\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/5/2554b6496c3b678897e9b060ef00aa9f0a7d7ece.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> all denote distinct digits from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/2/bf2c9074b396e3af0dea52d792660eea1c77f10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/4/e/a4ea1b248c8879f9eafa9a2be89a04279451ff7e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{STARS} = SAT$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"145\" height=\"21\" />, what are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/9/7/9970c215805f82282067d60741f7d2625e4d6a0c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A, R, S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"55\" height=\"16\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/5/2554b6496c3b678897e9b060ef00aa9f0a7d7ece.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" />? \n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_UNM-PNM_Statewide_High_School_Mathematics_Contest_II_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2017 UNM-PNM Statewide High School Mathematics Contest II Problems/Problem 2\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_3\">Problem 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_UNM-PNM_Statewide_High_School_Mathematics_Contest_II_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/9/9e9b01e32ab1f00dceffbf6199f0a25d1a451bb2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x)=\\frac{x}{x-1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"103\" height=\"33\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/4/f548915ecbe42087258ec53873c8c182ea9b2a5e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g(x)=\\frac{x}{3x-1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"111\" height=\"33\" />. \n</p><p>(a) Determine <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/7/d/77de3602095d356b693a8affff2f66d92baa1b94.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f\\circ g(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"60\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/2/0f2149a3a77f823a303d09cd0f617eac6b751b65.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g\\circ f(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"60\" height=\"18\" />. \n</p><p>(b) Denote <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/6/8/d6820b2221a441fe5be0da11057b41c91721d5c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\underbrace{h\\circ h\\circ \\cdot \\circ h}_\\text{n times} := h^n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"136\" height=\"35\" />. \nDetermine all the functions in the set <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/5/17578c8a6678db4786e6541ee3aff70230fa91ba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S = \\{H | H = (g\\circ f)^n\\circ g$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"194\" height=\"18\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/c/9/5c9141fc7f10c58675063bcfc2cfa6fe33cb988b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$H = (f\\circ g)^n\\circ f$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"129\" height=\"18\" /> for some <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> a whole number<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/e/65e2585c1b1cd632b41a41481fd2ad44456aeec4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"8\" height=\"18\" />. \n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_UNM-PNM_Statewide_High_School_Mathematics_Contest_II_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2017 UNM-PNM Statewide High School Mathematics Contest II Problems/Problem 3\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_4\">Problem 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_UNM-PNM_Statewide_High_School_Mathematics_Contest_II_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Find a second-degree polynomial with integer coeﬃcients, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/3/e/23e15593ac563c6b655cd4217872c4efb215d22c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p(x) = ax^2 + bx + c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"157\" height=\"19\" />, such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/a/f1a39d5d513f9d86d5a6afe686813bdbbfdb76a1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p(1),p(3),p(5)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"112\" height=\"18\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/b/a7b68248c8649cab41ecd3efbc9f1782ecce06b5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p(7)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"34\" height=\"20\" /> are perfect squares, but <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/1/b/e1b5a39632eb09829e575edc9b05b8f39401abcb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p(2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"31\" height=\"18\" /> is not. \n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_UNM-PNM_Statewide_High_School_Mathematics_Contest_II_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2017 UNM-PNM Statewide High School Mathematics Contest II Problems/Problem 4\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_5\">Problem 5</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_UNM-PNM_Statewide_High_School_Mathematics_Contest_II_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 5\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Find all real triples <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/3/c73ed093cc73a8d9a14185fa525e7067e5c3725d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x,y,z)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"58\" height=\"18\" /> which are solutions to the system:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/a/c/0acc7cf8414d42f76fa843714f4034c6df55c33b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^3 + x^2y + x^2z = 40$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"158\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/b/1abe91b0e293974e90f029188f5553b416ed0ed6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y^3 + y^2x + y^2z = 90$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"157\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/7/b/e7bef18c48175da69cd2bf18158ef51f37edc32a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z^3 + z^2x + z^2y = 250$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"165\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_UNM-PNM_Statewide_High_School_Mathematics_Contest_II_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2017 UNM-PNM Statewide High School Mathematics Contest II Problems/Problem 5\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_6\">Problem 6</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_UNM-PNM_Statewide_High_School_Mathematics_Contest_II_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 6\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>There are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/f/edf074831eb5bc9e61d6d6e09f525a86e3068f6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> stacks of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/f/edf074831eb5bc9e61d6d6e09f525a86e3068f6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> coins. Each of the coins in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/8/c6878713578626763c38433b3f4c8c2205ad0c15.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$11$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> of the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/f/edf074831eb5bc9e61d6d6e09f525a86e3068f6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> stacks weighs <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> grams each. Suppose the coins in the remaining stack each weigh <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/2/4/d24a6676b044440199a3da3885a07fb0fb336b22.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9.9$\" width=\"22\" height=\"12\" /> grams. You are given one time access to a precise digital scale. Devise a plan to weigh some coins in precisely one weighing to determine which pile has the lighter coins. \n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_UNM-PNM_Statewide_High_School_Mathematics_Contest_II_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2017 UNM-PNM Statewide High School Mathematics Contest II Problems/Problem 6\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_7\">Problem 7</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_UNM-PNM_Statewide_High_School_Mathematics_Contest_II_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 7\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Find a formula for\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/0/d/20da502812c9992f10b0b45bf0e6248b69097ea5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sum_{k=0}^{\\lfloor \\frac{n}{4} \\rfloor } \\binom{n}{4k}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -22px\" width=\"72\" height=\"55\" /> for any natural number <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />. \n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_UNM-PNM_Statewide_High_School_Mathematics_Contest_II_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2017 UNM-PNM Statewide High School Mathematics Contest II Problems/Problem 7\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_8\">Problem 8</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_UNM-PNM_Statewide_High_School_Mathematics_Contest_II_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 8\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/4/0d4fb3befd32138ebd96c3e69941c940a1c7d0fb.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy]  pair C=(0,0),A=(0,12),B=(5,0); draw(C--A--B--C,dot); MP(&quot;A&quot;,A,N);MP(&quot;C&quot;,C,SW);MP(&quot;B&quot;,B,E);  real r=10/3; pair X=(0,r),Y=X+r*(12/13,5/13); draw(X--Y,dot); MP(&quot;X&quot;,X,W);MP(&quot;Y&quot;,Y,NE);  draw(circle(X,r));  MP(&quot;12&quot;,(0,8),W);MP(&quot;5&quot;,(2.5,0),S);  [/asy]\" width=\"172\" height=\"252\" />\n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" /> be a right triangle with right angle at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />. Suppose <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/6/d/d6ddf755b50701c255c065a1c2b6f40c089175d4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC = 12$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"69\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/8/8/18873ba5dae90bd0238752b4cf8a422fedc84cc6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC = 5$\" width=\"61\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/2/73205379672e860eb250c541187600fae3a3e225.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CX$\" width=\"30\" height=\"12\" /> is the diameter of a semicircle, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/4/6a47ca0fe7cb276abc022af6ac88ddae1a9d6894.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> lies on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/7/a179ff2638e4799cadd820db205c2beff6299ce9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> and the semicircle is tangent to side <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" />. Find the radius of the semicircle.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_UNM-PNM_Statewide_High_School_Mathematics_Contest_II_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2017 UNM-PNM Statewide High School Mathematics Contest II Problems/Problem 8\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_9\">Problem 9</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_UNM-PNM_Statewide_High_School_Mathematics_Contest_II_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 9\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Consider a triangulation (mesh) of a polygonal domain like the one in the ﬁgure below. (a) Given the vertices of a triangle, devise a strategy for determining if a given point is inside that triangle. (b) Will your strategy work for polygons with more than three sides? (c) After implementing your strategy in an optimally eﬃcient computer code you ﬁnd that the search for a problem with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/9/e59e2c6e83eb78cca610a5fd4070ae01c8d4ae60.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$100$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" /> triangles, on average, takes <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> seconds. You reﬁne the triangulation by subdividing each of the triangles into smaller triangles by placing a new vertex at the center of gravity of each triangle. On average, how long will it take to ﬁnd a point in the new mesh?\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_UNM-PNM_Statewide_High_School_Mathematics_Contest_II_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2017 UNM-PNM Statewide High School Mathematics Contest II Problems/Problem 9\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_10\">Problem 10</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_UNM-PNM_Statewide_High_School_Mathematics_Contest_II_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=10\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 10\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Newton’s method applied to the equation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/0/d/b0df624702c1f988d1b966737e9c46c03bd39eb1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x) = x^3-x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"109\" height=\"19\" /> takes the form of the iteration <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/8/8/8885a96b8f00b77a367c1a24db191d1cedf738e5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_{n+1} =x_n-\\frac{(x_n)^3-x_n}{3{x_n}^2-1} , n = 0,1,2,\\ldots$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"303\" height=\"41\" />\n</p><p>(a) What are the roots of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/c/57ccf8d123ba4259e29fba55d9b008874e071492.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x) = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"68\" height=\"18\" />? \n</p><p>(b) Study the behavior of the iteration when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/3/313f1bc49fedd53375f2bf1392783230cea7989a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_0 &gt; \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"68\" height=\"41\" /> to conclude that the sequence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/5/69551c3500bc3d72e8da62cb464c89b4ff8c54c4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\{x_0,x_1,\\ldots\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"90\" height=\"18\" /> approaches the same root as long as you choose <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/3/313f1bc49fedd53375f2bf1392783230cea7989a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_0 &gt; \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"68\" height=\"41\" />. It may be helpful to start with the case <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/2/fc271598aa425b1f006e6db4fa5dfa0e90f8e7e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_0&gt;1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"50\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>(c) Assume <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/4/904d8adba8430da264ef4946399ec7e14486a035.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-\\alpha &lt; x_0 &lt; \\alpha$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"106\" height=\"15\" />. For what number <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/f/10f32377ac67d94f764f12a15ea987e88c85d3e1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\alpha$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" /> does the sequence always approach <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />?\n</p><p>(d) For <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/b/36bb2bc18eebc8db8e9490c2526747cc79ee10c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_0 \\in(\\alpha,\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"100\" height=\"41\" /> the sequence may approach either of the roots <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/c/c9c7695aa4cd5bf92c7da668b766fdfe244a113a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\pm x^{*}$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"30\" height=\"13\" />. Can you ﬁnd an (implicit) expression that can be used to determine limits <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/2/412787c048e28774dc63fc27db42dc52ca858de7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/c/bac5179cf12e1a7ff085b57db0ca3f9d9c2e6e9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{i+1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"29\" height=\"12\" /> such that if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/1/2/6129d38d496e99f6410e09e6e0d18f42257c4034.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x0 \\in (a_i,a_{i+1})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"109\" height=\"18\" /> then the sequence approaches <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/4/5549be72a072b90b44c61e9f513388766bc6f199.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(-1)^i{x^{*}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"59\" height=\"19\" />. Hint:<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/f/f8fe8abbe2edf8c2677bc17eb0a981830eb12397.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1 = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}, a_i &gt; a_{i+1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"146\" height=\"41\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/2/412787c048e28774dc63fc27db42dc52ca858de7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" /> approaches <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/e/2/ae26d1d19e9371dd57975f8cc1eb7c580626ad25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"30\" height=\"43\" /> when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/8/34857b3ba74ce5cd8607f3ebd23e9015908ada71.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"14\" /> becomes large.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_UNM-PNM_Statewide_High_School_Mathematics_Contest_II_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2017 UNM-PNM Statewide High School Mathematics Contest II Problems/Problem 10\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_UNM-PNM_Statewide_High_School_Mathematics_Contest_II_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=11\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018061701\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.031 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.043 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 363/1000000\nPost‐e